WEBVTT

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.320
You have quite an appetite, so early 
in the morning, Mr. Tokumatsu.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.160
You bet I do!

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.660
Food tastes best after a great duel.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.690
Now, you guys eat up, too.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.630
This is delicious, unlike that stuff...

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.860
Let's eat!

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.000
Give me a break!

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.980
I wasn't involved!

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.660
Just come along.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.030
No! Stop it!

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.440
Give me a break!

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.180
It seems some of his friends tried to break out.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.380
Break out?

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.580
What a stupid thing to do...

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.050
They should consider the fate of friends left behind.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.240
What do you mean?

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.120
When something like this happens,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.030
all the people left behind share 
responsibility and punishment.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.070
Punishment?

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.410
Wherever they're taken, no one's ever come back.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.620
D-Wheels.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:02.840
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.520
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.140
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.350
The Great Entertainment Duel Tournament!!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.420
A card?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.320
This is... Crow's...

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.850
Hey, Yuya! I'm counting on you again tomorrow!

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.600
What, I'm on cleaning duty again tomorrow?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.370
No, I wanted to see another duel like yesterday's,

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.280
so I had a talk with Mr. Tokumatsu.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.340
He said doing it in front of a big crowd 
would make it even more exciting,

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.050
so I talked with the warden.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:23.880
Tomorrow, in the dining hall, we'll have 
a big entertainment duel tournament!

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.380
In which case,

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.400
that sounds like my cue.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.470
You seem awfully confident, little man.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.440
You bet I am.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.260
Well, I'll let you stay that way 
until I pulverize you tomorrow.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:37.690
Crow!

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.970
This is yours, right?

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.650
Did Shinji tell you?

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.330
About the duel?

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.400
Go ahead and enjoy that.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.740
And...

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.540
Starting today, we're not allies.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.920
You aren't considering anything crazy, are you?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.420
I owe Shinji a favor.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.390
I'll work with him.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.050
Crow...

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.130
I won't make any trouble for you.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.630
Hey, Crow!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.820
Doing okay?

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.190
Damon!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.390
I came by your house to hang out.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.570
Oh, come on...

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.330
Hey, so you got caught?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.810
Weren't you posting the weird fliers with that girl?

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.550
About some kind of invasion 
from another dimension?

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.520
You mean...

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.980
Yuzu?

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.820
Yuzu was doing that?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.990
What about the girl? Was she caught?

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:48.200
Yeah, I guess security had it out for both of you...

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.600
Well, Crow, see you later.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.490
Yeah.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.060
Security's after Yuzu?

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.140
I have a report.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:02.200
We've confirmed the two wanted fugitives

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.620
among the applicants for the Friendship Cup.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.650
Oh, so they came to us?

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.500
Excellent.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.440
Give them permission.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.610
Yes, sir.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.880
If I arrest them both at the Friendship Cup venue,

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.880
it will set a good example for the Commons.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.270
Go on.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.480
That was Rin's room. You can use it for a while.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.540
Is that all right?

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.170
I think so... You can wear 
some of her clothes, too.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.040
As far as I can tell, you probably 
wear the same size.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.630
Besides, that outfit will stink 
if you wear it too much!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.400
Why are you telling a girl that?!

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.820
You've got no delicacy! You stink!

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:54.710
Sorry... Ma'am, please let her 
wash up, too, okay?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.080
That was heaven!

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:11.530
Rin!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.520
I get it. You're Yuzu, right? Yuzu!

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:21.630
Are you serious?

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:25.600
You bet. I'll win the Friendship Cup.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.650
That was the promise I made to Rin.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.260
I submitted one for you, too.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.810
For me?!

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.380
Making your appeal in front of a big crowd

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:41.180
will do a lot more to inform people about the invasion

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.280
than putting up those fliers. Right?

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.460
Jeez...

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.520
One, two...

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.800
Put your backs into it, men!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.400
Mr. Tokumatsu's pretty excited, huh?

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.100
Take care, okay?

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.670
You, too, Yuya.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.390
If Hugo isn't here, Yuzu's probably still okay, but...

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.040
If security is after her...

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.290
Crow... Hey, Crow.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.550
If you're thinking about getting out of here,

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.050
could I come, too?

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.730
Don't act like we're friends. 
I told you we aren't allies.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.820
You should take better care of your own.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.250
Crow!

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:46.900
I got my disk back!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.650
Duels are akin to life!

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.860
You only live once.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.330
You win sometimes, and you lose sometimes.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.890
Don't be ashamed of defeat. 
Don't be complacent in victory.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.930
In other words, let's enjoy!

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.140
Enjoy!

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.360
It really is Enjoy Chojiro!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.610
He's back!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:19.630
And invigorated by a certain youngster.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:21.310
Right, Yuya Sakaki?

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:25.980
Come up here.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.330
He looks kind of nervous...

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.980
Having three of us here means 
a battle royal, right?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.840
Whatever you want.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.980
But let's kick it up a notch.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:01.420
How about the ultimate evolution 
of dueling, an Action Duel?

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:02.490
What's that?

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:08.090
We activate an Action Field, and use 
Action Cards spread about the field.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:09.960
Sounds interesting!

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.090
Then, let's do it.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:14.220
Action Field, on!

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.900
Field Spell Crossover.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.750
The duelists meet at the battlefield.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.800
Hey!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.340
A-Along with their monsters, they'll kick 
the ground and fly through the sky

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.290
to move around the field!

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.650
Witness dueling's greatest evolution.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.030
Action...

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:39.480
Duel!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.570
My turn!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.990
First, I'll show you how Action Cards work!

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.370
What are you doing?

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.290
Even if you can't draw or battle, you can 
use Action Cards on the first turn.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:01.830
I activate my Action Spell Illumination!

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:05.790
Let's make our stage shine with sparkling colors!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.640
Incidentally, for this turn,

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.620
monster summoning and Special 
Summoning is not negated.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:16.190
I'll show you some creatures 
you've never seen before.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:23.290
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1 
Evil Heel and Scale 8 Funky Comedian!

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.570
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.310
So you can use that, too?

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.330
Pendulum Summon!

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:40.320
Come out, Level 7 Superstar!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.060
He brought out a high-level monster 
without a Synchro Summon?

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:47.260
Yeah, that's how Pendulum Summon works.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.800
Now, let's pick up the excitement even more.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:55.770
I activate my Continuous Spell Abyss Stage — 
Treasure Boat of the Lucky Seven!

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:02.570
During their turn, all players once can 
put one monster on this boat,

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:05.820
destroying all other monsters on their field.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.760
Superstar, get on the treasure boat!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.960
Now, who else wants to ride it?

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.450
It's a great way to earn money!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.830
I end my turn.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.030
Do you think it'll work?

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:30.230
Yeah, no problem.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.700
Hey...

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.560
Aren't you done yet?

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.910
What are you doing?

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:42.620
The fan wasn't working, so we're fixing it.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.620
He's good at that kind of thing.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.430
I see. Well, hurry it up.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.820
The duel's going to end without you.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.300
Okay!

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.200
Not bad at all.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:00.700
My turn.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:04.000
Enjoy!

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.240
There he is! The big boss!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.740
Enjoy!

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.920
I'm gonna enjoy this Action Duel.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:15.530
Action Spell Sound Rebound!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.360
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.780
Let's enjoy!

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:24.770
Just once this turn, a spell card 
effect can't be negated.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:27.120
But I don't care about that.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:30.780
When entertaining people, this lively 
atmosphere is what's important!

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.670
I activate Super Koi Koi from my hand!

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.120
I draw three cards from my deck.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:42.310
If there are Flower Cardians among them, 
I can Special Summon them all.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:46.540
But any non-Cardians you draw 
are sent to the graveyard,

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:50.750
and for each, you take 1000 damage.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.290
If I didn't try to enjoy this, I'd have 
to abandon my name.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.490
Now, then... Come on!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:59.720
Come on, come on, come on!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.460
Come on, come on, come on!

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:05.560
The first one is Flower Cardian Clover with Boar.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.500
The second... Come on, come on!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.770
Come on, come on!

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.500
The second is Flower Cardian Maple with Deer!

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.180
His draws are as strong as ever!

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.470
You bet they are.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:20.300
And the last one! Come on, come on... 
Come on, come on!

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.310
The last is Flower Cardian Peony with Butterfly!

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.530
The effect of Special Summoning them is that 
their attack and defense points all become 0,

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.380
and their levels become 2!

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:35.520
Level 2 Peony with Butterfly

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:39.720
tunes Clover with Boar and Maple with Deer!

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:45.100
The courage of the boar, the elegance of the deer,

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.810
the beauty of the butterfly!

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.740
Synchro Summon!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.780
Level 6 Flower Cardian Boardefly!

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.190
I'll follow your good fortune!

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:06.360
Get on the treasure boat, Boardefly!

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:11.560
Not a bad show at all, old man!

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.800
You'd better believe it!

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.120
Now, I end my turn.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.420
Well, Yuya? It's your turn next.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.940
Hey, Yuya...

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:37.070
My turn. Draw!

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:40.550
I summon Performapal Hip Hippo!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.650
I have to get out, too. For Yuzu.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.960
You should take better care of your own.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:10.970
I set a card and end my turn.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:16.160
Hey, what's with you? Didn't you 
come here to enjoy yourself?

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:22.250
Weren't you the one who fought that legendary duel 
with me at the Maiami City Championship?

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.380
Yuya...

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.550
This wasn't the deal.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.370
What do you mean, it wasn't the deal?

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.340
Tell me more.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.050
This isn't satisfying at all...

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:41.120
Then, I'll have to make a comeback!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:44.660
My turn! I activate Treasure Boat 
of the Lucky Seven's effect!

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:49.630
I can draw as many extra cards as 
I have monsters on the boat.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.760
I draw two cards!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.570
So that's the fortune you reap from it?

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.000
That's right...

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.500
But that alone won't satisfy me...

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:05.210
Not only did you draw two cards, 
but you want Action Cards, too?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.210
You're a greedy one.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:11.290
If you don't like it, keep up with me, 
old man. You, too, Yuya.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.460
That's right, Yuya!

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.380
Get moving!

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:19.160
Gongenzaka?

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.040
No need to worry.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:25.360
Hi!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:29.000
You go ahead and do what you need to do!

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.740
We'll do what we need to do.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.350
The fun is only getting started!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.850
So you're finally ready to enjoy it?

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.790
Quick-Play Spell Hippo Carnival!

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.560
S-Stay back, you stupid hippos!

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.830
Let's go, Hippo!

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.240
You won't beat me!

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.900
It's a race to the Action Card!

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.730
What's he doing?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.200
Hey, kid... Are you all ri—

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.300
Hey, what are you guys doing?

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.210
He escaped?

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.350
Hey, you!

00:17:58.690 --> 00:17:59.880
You, eh?

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.460
What are you doing?

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:04.920
What do you think? I came to save you.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:06.740
I didn't need your help.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:08.520
Let's go.

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.900
Hey, where are you going?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:19.940
Who's there?

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:22.310
You're...

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:26.050
I've come to save the captive princess.

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:28.630
Your hand, my lady.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.020
It's a jailbreak!

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.260
Cancel the duel!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.230
Everyone, stay right where you are!

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.670
Hey, Crow!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:45.040
Hey, you... A jailbreak is a serious crime.

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:47.940
You get that, don't you?

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.780
Time for your punishment—

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:12.120
Battle!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:21.370
What is he doing?

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.110
You're under arrest...

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:36.230
Go over there to enjoy yourself!

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.400
Hey, we don't have time for nonsense—

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.540
You want to try to escape unarmed?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:53.900
Out of the way!

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:54.950
Who are you?

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:58.950
Mr. Tokumatsu!

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:03.980
Brat, you used a duel as a cover for this?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:06.280
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:11.660
I'm sorry, Mr. Tokumatsu. I did it to save Yuzu!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:18.810
Yuzu's working so hard to inform this 
world about the coming danger.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:22.200
Because of that, security is after her.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:23.400
That's why...

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.370
Go on.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.310
Stay right where you are!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:33.700
Mr. Tokumatsu!

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:36.650
I owe you. I'm repaying it here.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.820
Be well.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.290
Out of the way, Tokumatsu!

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:45.020
A rare card!

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.280
Amazing... This one's super rare!

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:53.180
Now, now! Here's today's main event!

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:57.900
Enjoy Chojiro's big comeback giveaway!

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.180
Boss!

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:14.390
Return to the stage of the outside world!

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:17.100
Boss, take care!

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:18.860
Those guys...

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.290
Come on, more where that came from!

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:24.540
Come on!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.000
If that's what you want, I'll do it!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.030
Let's go, Yuya.

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:33.030
Yeah!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:34.740
Let's go, Sawatari!

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.340
Right!

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:40.340
I activate my Action Card Curtain Clap!

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:52.060
Are you sure this is okay? 
There's no turning back now.

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:54.180
You can't go wrong, following me.

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:57.500
A world of freedom unfurls ahead of us!

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:01.350
Hey, this is the roof! And those are...

00:24:01.350 --> 00:24:03.720
We can distract those guards with rare cards.

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:08.110
It's no use... They're a special team 
formed to catch jail breakers.

00:24:08.110 --> 00:24:10.460
They won't be distracted by rare cards.

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:14.970
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
King of the Captors. Goyo King.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.100
The fun is only getting started!
